TI  - [Malignant pleural effusion].
LID - V10200751 [pii]
AB  - Malignant pleural effusion (MPE) is a common condition, often associated with a 
      high level of symptoms. In this review, several palliative treatments for 
      symptomatic MPE are summarised, including repeated thoracentesis, pleurodesis and 
      insertion of indwelling pleural catheters. Choice of treatment depends on patient 
      symptoms, life expectancy, pleural fluid production, expected effect of 
      oncological treatment, whether trapped lung is suspected or not, and patient 
      preferences. Treatment should be discussed with a pulmonary specialist with 
      knowledge of pleural diseases.
