TI  - Novel complications of the tunnelled indwelling pleural catheter.
PG  - 166-168
LID - S2531-0437(19)30203-X [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.pulmoe.2019.08.008 [doi]
AB  - Tunnelled indwelling pleural catheters (TIPC) are a modality of treatment for 
      malignant pleural effusions. Though relatively easy, safe and efficacious, they 
      are associated with a small risk of complications. We describe newer 
      complications of the TIPC including the retention of the polyester plug and the 
      blockage of the catheter with thick organised material consisting of malignant 
      cells taking the shape of the catheter.
